      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think one problem is that Ganesh has a `SkSL::SampleUsage` field on its fragment processors, but we don\u0027t have that for ShaderSnippets or ShaderNodes. And since its determined by a node\u0027s parent, it\u0027s a little inconvenient to define statically in ShaderSnippets.\n\nMy current idea to address that was to have a field on ShaderSnippet of per-child flags designating how the snippet\u0027s coordinates are passed to children, and then set a \"how am I sampled\" field on the ShaderNodes while building the node tree, based on these per-child flags in the snippets. But that idea added enough complexity that I uploaded this all-or-nothing approach to begin with.",
      "parentUuid": "e1e076d4_12ec1e4d",
